  "guideBody1": "If a prediction has a 75% probability, the model expects it to come true about 3 times out of 4 when a similar situation repeats. That means 1 in 4 will not. No data guarantees a specific result.",
  "guideBody2": "Odds are set by a bookmaker and include its margin. Comparing the model's probability with the one implied by the odds helps you judge whether the price is reasonable; it does not ensure the result.",
  "guideBody3": "They are published with their probability and reference odds before kickoff and cannot be edited. That is why you can compare the real historical hit rate with the promised one.",
  "guideBody4": "In a parlay, the joint probability is the product of each selection's, so it drops quickly as you add matches. A high price usually reflects exactly that.",
  "guideBody5": "Each challenge goes in steps and the next one only counts if the previous one is met. Check the progress and the history, failed challenges included, before following one.",
